From: LightMoss <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gamecontroller: add automatic mappings without the name CRC

When SDL opens a joystick it has no mapping for, it makes one from the
device's evdev buttons and adds it with the CRC of the device's name
("crc:xxxx"). A mapping with the device's CRC is an exact match, which
SDL_PrivateMatchControllerMappingForGUID returns before any mapping
without a CRC. So a mapping added later without one, whatever its
priority, never applies to that device: in particular a
gamecontrollerdb.txt row that a program loads after SDL_Init, when the
joysticks present have already been added (SDL_PrivateJoystickAdded
calls SDL_IsGameController, which makes the automatic mapping).

That is how PPSSPP loads its database, and on the R36S clone the
automatic mapping of the "GO-Super Gamepad" has no back, start, guide
or stick buttons (BTN_TRIGGER_HAPPY1-5), so PPSSPP saw neither Select
nor Start and could not bind them, while its database row for the pad
has them. dArkMoss, whose behaviour spruce is written for, builds SDL
with the controller code from before the CRC change, where the row
replaces the automatic mapping.

Add the automatic mapping without the CRC, so that a later mapping for
the device's GUID replaces it as before. Mappings that carry a CRC
themselves (from a GUID string with one, or "crc:" in the mapping) are
matched as before.

diff --git a/src/joystick/SDL_gamecontroller.c b/src/joystick/SDL_gamecontroller.c
index 36e521e..bc17807 100644
--- a/src/joystick/SDL_gamecontroller.c
+++ b/src/joystick/SDL_gamecontroller.c
@@ -1462,6 +1462,12 @@ static ControllerMapping_t *SDL_PrivateGenerateAutomaticControllerMapping(const
     SDL_PrivateAppendToMappingString(mapping, sizeof(mapping), "righttrigger", &raw_map->righttrigger);
     SDL_PrivateAppendToMappingString(mapping, sizeof(mapping), "touchpad", &raw_map->touchpad);
 
+    /* Add the automatic mapping without the device name's CRC. With it, the
+     * mapping is an exact match that beats every mapping added later without
+     * a CRC (a gamecontrollerdb.txt row, which a program loads after
+     * SDL_Init, when SDL has already made this one), whatever its priority.
+     * Without it, such a mapping replaces this one, as before SDL 2.26. */
+    SDL_SetJoystickGUIDCRC(&guid, 0);
     return SDL_PrivateAddMappingForGUID(guid, mapping, &existing, SDL_CONTROLLER_MAPPING_PRIORITY_DEFAULT);
 }
 
